# P3-1: psa-kali build context exclusions.
#
# Keeping the build context small matters because
# `docker build` uploads the entire context to the
# daemon before processing. The psa-kali image only
# needs the Dockerfile, the entrypoint script, and
# this .dockerignore.
#
# Anything below is matched by Go's filepath.Match
# semantics (not regex). Patterns are case-sensitive
# on Linux.

# Editor / OS junk
**/.DS_Store
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# The MANIFEST.md and README.md are documentation for
# humans, not build inputs. The Dockerfile doesn't
# COPY them. Keeping them out of the context cuts the
# upload by ~15 KB.
MANIFEST.md
README.md
build.sh

# Anything not explicitly COPY'd by the Dockerfile.
# Defense in depth — if a future change accidentally
# adds `COPY . .` we'd skip the build-arg variants
# below anyway, but excluding here makes the
# blast-radius explicit.
*.go
*.c
*.h
*.o
*.a
*.so
go.mod
go.sum

# Test outputs that might be lying around
**/coverage.out
**/coverage.html
**/*.test
**/*.prof

# VCS metadata
**/.gitattributes
**/.github
